Package: GLproxScape
Type: Package
Title: Spatial Reconstruction of Chromatin Occupancy from Tiled Genomic Locus Proteomics
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: person(given = "Can",
                  family = "Ozcan",
                  role = c("aut", "cre"),
                  email = "s.canozcan89@gmail.com")
Description: Spatial analysis of tiled genomic locus proteomics data
    (dCas9-APEX2 / CASPEX, GLoPro and related designs). Models each sgRNA's
    biotinylation footprint as a Gaussian labeling kernel and converts
    per-region enrichments into a coverage-normalized spatial signal, on which
    transcription factor binding events are called at motif sites (JASPAR,
    HOCOMOCO v12 or CIS-BP 3.10 position weight matrices; human, mouse and,
    through CIS-BP, other species), with a motif-free path for factors without
    a motif and zone-based detection for chromatin regulators. Optional
    ChIP-Atlas overlay for independent peak support (including tagged
    pulldowns and cell-type-matched experiments), locus-level histone marks,
    and cell-line expression annotation from the Human Protein Atlas.
